# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Ryan M. Jacobs et al. (2025). A practical guide to machine learning interatomic potentials – Status and future.
#   Current Opinion in Solid State and Materials Science. doi:10.1016/j.cossms.2025.101214  arXiv:2503.09814v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2503.09814v1 (sha256 1ef4fbe54f2d7cd3...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 9 (Overview/taxonomy). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: bibliographic facts only. The article is a long
# practical review: a list of MLIPs, the basic formalisms (explicit and
# implicit atomic-environment featurisation), universal MLIPs, execution
# speed, how to choose or fit a potential, infrastructure, limits and
# outlook. It trains no model and reports no result of its own that the
# schema can carry. Read from the arXiv preprint (v1).

